    content: `The Biological Diversity Act, 2002 (amended 2023) and BD Rules 2024 govern access to biological resources and associated traditional knowledge. STRUCTURE: Three-tier system — National Biodiversity Authority (NBA), State Biodiversity Boards (SBBs), Biodiversity Management Committees (BMCs) at local level. KEY PROVISIONS: (1) Section 3: Foreign persons/entities/NRIs require PRIOR APPROVAL from NBA before obtaining biological resources or associated TK for research, commercial utilization, or bio-survey. Penalty: imprisonment up to 5 years, fine up to Rs.10 lakh. (2) Section 4: Transfer results of research to foreign persons — needs NBA approval. (3) Section 5: Collaborative research with foreign institutions — needs NBA approval. (4) Section 6: Indian persons/entities must give PRIOR INTIMATION to SBB before obtaining biological resources for commercial utilization. New in 2023 Amendment: Section 7 now requires only intimation (not approval) for Indian persons accessing biological resources for commercial use. (5) Section 6(1): Anyone seeking ANY IP right based on research/information on Indian biological resources must obtain prior approval from NBA. Non-compliance: IP right not granted or if granted, can be revoked. (6) 2023 AMENDMENT KEY CHANGES: (a) Exempts registered AYUSH practitioners using codified TK; (b) Exempts cultivated medicinal plants (with conditions); (c) Decriminalizes certain offences (civil penalties instead of criminal); (d) Simplifies compliance for Indian users; (e) Promotes Indian systems of medicine; (f) Allows compounding of offences. (7) 2024 RULES: Digital application portal, standardized forms, timeline for decisions (6 months), percentage-based benefit sharing.`,
