    ipType: "patent",
    content: `COMPLETE PATENT FILING PROCEDURE FOR AYUSH INNOVATIONS: Step 1: PRIOR ART SEARCH — Search Indian Patent Office database (ipindiaservices.gov.in/publicsearch), Espacenet, Google Patents, PubMed, and request TKDL check if traditional knowledge is involved. Step 2: DRAFTING — Prepare provisional or complete specification with claims. For Ayurvedic inventions, emphasize what is novel beyond TK. Include experimental data showing inventive step. Step 3: FILE APPLICATION — File Form 1 (application), Form 2 (specification), Form 3 (statement of undertaking), Form 5 (declaration of inventorship). Declare biological material source. Declare TK source if applicable. Step 4: PUBLICATION — Application published 18 months from priority date (or earlier on request with Form 9). Step 5: EXAMINATION — Request examination within 48 months (Form 18). For startups, request expedited examination (Form 18A). Step 6: FIRST EXAMINATION REPORT (FER) — Respond within 6 months. Controller may raise Section 3(d), 3(e), 3(p) objections for Ayurvedic inventions. Step 7: HEARING — If objections persist, attend hearing. Step 8: GRANT — If all requirements met, patent granted for 20 years from filing. Step 9: RENEWAL — Pay annual renewal fees (Forms 4). FEES: Individual/startup: Rs. 1,600 (e-filing). Small entity: Rs. 4,000. Others: Rs. 8,000.`,
