    content: `Health Canada regulates Ayurvedic products as Natural Health Products (NHPs) under the Natural Health Products Regulations (NHPR). KEY REQUIREMENTS: (1) PRODUCT LICENSE: Apply through Natural and Non-prescription Health Products Directorate (NNHPD). Submit Product License Application (PLA). Evidence of safety and efficacy required — can use traditional use evidence for products with 50+ years of use. (2) SITE LICENSE: Manufacturing site must hold a Health Canada site license or equivalent recognized certification. (3) QUALITY: Good Manufacturing Practices per NHP Regulations Part 3. Specifications for identity, purity, potency. Stability testing. (4) LABELING: Must comply with NHPR labeling requirements. Bilingual (English/French) required. NPN (Natural Product Number) must be displayed. (5) CLAIMS: Can make health claims supported by evidence. Traditional use claims accepted. (6) IP STRATEGY: File trademark through Madrid or directly with CIPO. Consider Canadian patent filing through PCT national phase.`,
